  "paragraph": "A mathematical page should read with the calm rhythm of a well-set book. Letters, figures and punctuation share the same light, while their varied shapes give each line its movement. A narrow counter must stay open; a fine stroke must survive at reading size. The italic turns within the roman texture without breaking it. In a companion mathematics family, Greek letters and symbols should feel at home beside these words, with clear distinctions and a consistent balance of black and white.",
